file:       mikktspace.c (master, read 2026-11-12)

What is here:
  Nothing but the licence. crates/shape-tools/src/mikk.rs is a port of
  mikktspace.c: an altered version (the licence asks that this be said).
  It is for triangles only (the reference's quad handling is left out),
  in f64 with this project's deterministic maths, with ordered maps in
  place of the reference's hashing and sorting; a triangle with two
  corners at one position takes the tangent of another corner at the
  same vertex, and a corner no group reaches keeps no tangent (the
  caller gives it one square to its normal).

Checked against Blender's MikkTSpace: Khronos' NormalTangentMirrorTest
(written by Blender's glTF exporter, CC-BY 4.0, not kept here), its
15 720 corners' tangents from the file's positions, normals and UVs:
the largest angle to the file's TANGENT 0.03 degrees, every sign equal.
